{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-2351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=2{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+2t$, where $t$ is measured in seconds.  Find the particle's acceleration at $t=2$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-2351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+2t) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}-6t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}-6t+2) \\\\  & =12t-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=2$, we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(2) & =12(2)-6 \\\\  & =24-6 \\\\  & =18\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration when $t=2$ seconds is $18\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-2351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "55c18e5d2c00dd0f8b4e5a6a31c9bea58645fa1d57354713849e3c370b9900e1"} {"question" "q-2351" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-2351" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "14\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "18\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "21\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "24\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-2351" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-7101" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The displacement $s$ of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=3-6{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}.$ Find the particle's acceleration at time $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-7101" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3-6{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =-12t+6{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-12t+6{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =-12+12t \\\\  & =12(t-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-7101" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "55c18e5d2c00dd0f8b4e5a6a31c9bea58645fa1d57354713849e3c370b9900e1"} {"question" "q-7101" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-7101" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a(t)=12(2-t)"] ["math" "a(t)=12(t+1)"] ["math" "a(t)=12(t-1)"] ["math" "a(t)=6t(t+2)"] ["math" "a(t)=6t(t-2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-7101" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a(t)=12(t-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-7186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity $v$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{t}.$ Calculate the acceleration of the particle at time $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-7186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-\\frac{1}{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-{t}^{-1}) \\\\  & =1-(-{t}^{-2}) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-7186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "55c18e5d2c00dd0f8b4e5a6a31c9bea58645fa1d57354713849e3c370b9900e1"} {"question" "q-7186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-7186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a(t)=1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}"] ["math" "a(t)=1-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}"] ["math" "a(t)=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}"] ["math" "a(t)=t+\\frac{1}{t}"] ["math" "a(t)=t-\\frac{1}{t}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-7186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a(t)=1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-336423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=2{t}^{4}-3{t}^{2}+t,$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Calculate the acceleration of the particle at $t=1$ second.\n\n$a(1)=$\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-336423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{4}-3{t}^{2}+t) \\\\  & =8{t}^{3}-6t+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration when $t=1$ second, we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =8(1)^{3}-6(1)+1 \\\\  & =8-6+1 \\\\  & =3\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-336423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "55c18e5d2c00dd0f8b4e5a6a31c9bea58645fa1d57354713849e3c370b9900e1"} {"question" "q-336423" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-336423" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-336452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The displacement $s$ of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=5+3{t}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}.$ Find the particle's acceleration at time $t.$\n\n$a(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-336452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5+3{t}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =6t-{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6t-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =6-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709c1d9ce24b3163dc81a2c488d262e6b3ca802c3c00a2be"} {"question" "q-336452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "55c18e5d2c00dd0f8b4e5a6a31c9bea58645fa1d57354713849e3c370b9900e1"} {"question" "q-336452" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973858/state.json" "file_sha256" "43ec313245d39d1d709